🎯 Objective

This project implements a multi-threaded Python server using Flask to expose statistical APIs based on a public dataset about physical activity, nutrition, and obesity in the United States (2011–2022). The goal is to deepen understanding of:

    Synchronization mechanisms and multithreading in Python

    Flask framework and API development

    Data processing using pandas

    Logging and job queue management

    Graceful shutdown and concurrent processing patterns

🗂️ Dataset

The dataset, provided by the U.S. Department of Health & Human Services, includes yearly health and nutrition statistics per U.S. state. Each row contains:

    A state

    A question (e.g., "Percent of adults aged 18 years and older who have obesity")

    A Data_Value (percentage)

    Optional Stratification info for categories such as age, gender, education

🛠️ Implementation Overview

The server follows a job-based request model:

    Clients send a request (e.g., to compute state averages).

    A unique job_id is assigned and the job is placed in a job queue.

    A Thread Pool picks up jobs, processes them, and writes results to a file (results/job_id_x.json).

    Clients can query the job status/result using /api/get_results/<job_id>.

📁 Project Structure

    app/data_ingestor.py – Loads and filters the CSV data; contains all data processing functions.

    app/task_runner.py – Manages the thread pool and job queue.

    app/routes.py – Defines all Flask routes and handles request/response logic.

    app/logging.py – Sets up RotatingFileHandler to log all route access and operations in UTC format.

    unittests/TestWebserver.py – Unit tests for core functionality.

    results/ – Output directory for job results.

    nutrition_activity_obesity_usa_subset.csv/ – CSV data file.

    checker/checker.py – A checker to verify the functionality

    pylintrc – Coding style checker

🔗 Available API Endpoints

All endpoints accept and return JSON.
📈 Statistical Requests
Endpoint	Description
/api/states_mean	Mean per state (sorted), given a question
/api/state_mean	Mean for a single state
/api/best5 / /api/worst5	Top/bottom 5 states based on mean value
/api/global_mean	Overall average across all states
/api/diff_from_mean	State differences from global mean
/api/state_diff_from_mean	One state's difference from global mean
/api/mean_by_category	Mean values per category (StratificationCategory1)
/api/state_mean_by_category	Same as above, but for one state

🧵 Job Management
Endpoint	Description
/api/get_results/<job_id>	Check status or retrieve result
/api/jobs	List of all jobs and their status
/api/num_jobs	Number of remaining jobs in queue
/api/graceful_shutdown	Begin graceful shutdown (stop accepting new jobs, wait for queue to drain)
🧪 Testing & Running
Setup

python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt

Running

In first terminal:

source venv/bin/activate
make run_server

In a second terminal:

source venv/bin/activate
make run_tests

🧪 Logging

All route accesses and major events are logged to webserver.log, with UTC timestamps and rotating file size management. Logs include:

    Route calls with parameters

    Job creation and completion

    Errors encountered
